{
  "name": "pinky",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "gannet",
  "notes": "A pinky, the small pink-sterned fishing schooner of the bay, 13 m on deck and 3.8 m in the beam: slate-blue hull over a red bottom, white rail, the bulwarks carried aft into the high narrow pink with the tiller through it, two gaff-rigged masts with the sails furled on the booms, a short bowsprit, a cuddy forward with a stovepipe, the fish hold hatch amidships and barrels on deck. Bow to local -Z. The anchor is the waterline: place her with `\"height\": 0` for her 1.75 m draft.",
